From db3a695e51018e7943ecb2a749591e128ebdf4bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:14:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 21/35] bitproxy: Block mode per app; sniff strictly after all
 app rules

Block: a third mode next to VPN and Direct. Blocked apps get a reject
rule for their traffic and their DNS (no internet at all). Dashboard
rows use a VPN / Direct / Block selector under the app name, the app
picker has Block / Unblock in its menu, new-app notifications get a
Block action. Apps sharing a uid take the most restrictive mode.

Sniff order fix: with a domain list, sniff now comes after every app
rule, as the spec says; before, Direct apps were sniffed first, which
is what stalled TCP on the phone. The domain list therefore applies to
apps that are not in the list.
